cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "Certified Symmetry Discovery: Confidence Sets for Lie-Algebra Generators from Noisy, Limited Data"
abstract: >-
  Symmetry discovery by nullspace computation has no error control and inverts
  the burden of proof. SymCert recasts it as an equivalence test and gives
  closed-form confidence bounds on the equivariance defect that hold
  simultaneously over every candidate generator.
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kendiukhov/certified-symmetry-discovery"
authors:
  - given-names: Ihor
    family-names: Kendiukhov
    email: kenduhov.ig@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Institute of Medical Genetics and Applied Genomics, University of Tübingen"
keywords:
  - symmetry discovery
  - Lie algebra
  - equivalence testing
  - dynamical systems
  - equivariance
